# Multi-Instance COSMIC Applet Guidance

This applet may run multiple instances simultaneously in multi-monitor or multi-panel setups. Treat each instance as an independent process with its own state and resources.

## Design Rules
- Per-instance state: Keep all UI and runtime state inside the `Window` model in [src/window.rs](mdc:src/window.rs).
- No global singletons for mutable state. If shared, use read-only constants or config; otherwise prefer per-instance channels.
- Thread affinity: Wayland objects created in [src/idle_monitor.rs](mdc:src/idle_monitor.rs) must be used on the same thread. Use `IdleMonitor::spawn(...)` to own the connection and event queue on a dedicated thread per applet instance.
- Do not store Wayland handles (`Connection`, `EventQueue`, `QueueHandle`, protocol proxies) in `Window`. Create and use them only inside the background thread via `IdleMonitor::spawn(...)`.
- Message delivery: Communicate idle/resume events via per-instance `std::sync::mpsc::channel` to the `Window` instance. Do not share channels across instances.

## Instance Isolation Checklist
- Avoid static mut / global caches for UI state or `TimeEntry`.
- Do not store process-wide singletons for `wl_seat`, `ExtIdleNotifierV1`, or event queues.
- Ensure popup `Id`s are created per `Window` instance and not reused.
- When writing to files (prefs/logs), include instance-safe paths (e.g., per monitor or window id) or use OS temp dirs; avoid clobbering.
  - Example: `let path = std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("clockify_applet_{}", self.core.main_window_id().unwrap()));`

## Subscriptions & Timers
- Use `time::every(...)` per instance for ticks; keep work small to avoid jank.
- Typical cadence is 200–500 ms; drain channels and return quickly.
- Drain the per-instance idle channel inside `Message::Tick` to avoid blocking the UI thread.

## Debug & Logging
- Prefix logs with the applet window or instance id when possible to differentiate instances.
  - Example:
```
if let Some(id) = self.core.main_window_id() {
    eprintln!("[applet {:?}] {}", id, "Idle!");
}
```
- Keep stdout/stderr noise minimal; prefer structured messages for development.

## UI
- Use `autosize` and `Core`-provided `suggested_size`/`suggested_padding` for proper panel sizing.
- Return the applet style for transparency:
```
fn style(&self) -> Option<cosmic::iced_runtime::Appearance> {
    Some(cosmic::applet::style())
}
```